<div id="poster">
  <header class="poster-header">
    <h1>Bot Mitigation at Scale: Protecting Scientific Publishing Platforms</h1>
    <div class="subtitle">IEEE Symposium on Security and Privacy</div>
    <div class="venue">Case Study: Science.org / AAAS</div>
  </header>

  <section class="poster-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">The Bot Threat Landscape for Academic Publishers</h2>
    <div class="metrics-grid">
      <div class="metric-card highlight">
        <div class="value">47%</div>
        <div class="label">Bot Traffic Share</div>
        <div class="desc">of all internet traffic in 2024</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-card">
        <div class="value">30%</div>
        <div class="label">Malicious Bots</div>
        <div class="desc">of total bot traffic</div>
      </div>
      <div class="metric-card">
        <div class="value">1.2M</div>
        <div class="label">Daily Scraping Attempts</div>
        <div class="desc">before mitigation deployment</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="poster-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Challenge-Based Verification Pipeline</h2>
    <div class="pipeline-flow">
      <div class="pipeline-stage">
        <div class="stage-left">
          <div class="stage-number">1</div>
          <div class="stage-connector"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="stage-content">
          <div class="stage-info">
            <h4>Request Interception</h4>
            <p>Incoming HTTP request routed through CDN edge node</p>
          </div>
          <div class="stage-time">&lt;50ms</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-stage">
        <div class="stage-left">
          <div class="stage-number">2</div>
          <div class="stage-connector"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="stage-content">
          <div class="stage-info">
            <h4>Threat Scoring</h4>
            <p>IP reputation, TLS fingerprint, behavioral signals evaluated</p>
          </div>
          <div class="stage-time">~100ms</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-stage">
        <div class="stage-left">
          <div class="stage-number">3</div>
          <div class="stage-connector"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="stage-content">
          <div class="stage-info">
            <h4>Challenge Issuance</h4>
            <p>JavaScript or CAPTCHA challenge served if risk exceeds threshold</p>
          </div>
          <div class="stage-time">~500ms</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-stage">
        <div class="stage-left">
          <div class="stage-number">4</div>
          <div class="stage-connector"></div>
        </div>
        <div class="stage-content">
          <div class="stage-info">
            <h4>Verification Check</h4>
            <p>Client response validated; unique Ray ID assigned for tracing</p>
          </div>
          <div class="stage-time">~200ms</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="pipeline-stage">
        <div class="stage-left">
          <div class="stage-number">5</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stage-content">
          <div class="stage-info">
            <h4>Access Grant</h4>
            <p>Verified user forwarded to origin server with session token</p>
          </div>
          <div class="stage-time">&lt;50ms</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="pipeline-total">
      <span>Total latency for legitimate users: &lt;2 seconds | Automated scripts lacking JavaScript execution are blocked entirely</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="poster-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Performance and Security Outcomes</h2>
    <div class="outcomes-grid">
      <div class="outcome-card">
        <div class="icon">🛡</div>
        <div class="info">
          <h4>85%</h4>
          <p>Reduction in scraping attempts</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="outcome-card">
        <div class="icon">📈</div>
        <div class="info">
          <h4>99.97%</h4>
          <p>Uptime during bot surges</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="outcome-card">
        <div class="icon">👥</div>
        <div class="info">
          <h4>0.3%</h4>
          <p>Legitimate users with friction</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="outcome-card">
        <div class="icon">⚡</div>
        <div class="info">
          <h4>&lt;150ms</h4>
          <p>Added latency for verified sessions</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="comparison-table">
      <div class="comparison-header">
        <span>Metric</span>
        <span style="text-align:center">Before</span>
        <span style="text-align:center">After</span>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-row">
        <span class="metric-name">Daily Scraping Attempts</span>
        <span class="before">1.2M</span>
        <span class="after">180K</span>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-row">
        <span class="metric-name">Origin Server Load (CPU)</span>
        <span class="before">78%</span>
        <span class="after">42%</span>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-row">
        <span class="metric-name">Monthly User Complaints</span>
        <span class="before">1,200</span>
        <span class="after">340</span>
      </div>
      <div class="comparison-row">
        <span class="metric-name">Uptime During Bot Surges</span>
        <span class="before">98.5%</span>
        <span class="after">99.97%</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="poster-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usability vs. Security Trade-offs</h2>
    <div class="tradeoffs-grid">
      <div class="tradeoff-card">
        <h4>♿ Accessibility</h4>
        <p>Challenge pages must comply with WCAG 2.1 standards to avoid excluding users with disabilities.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tradeoff-card">
        <h4>🏛 Institutional Access</h4>
        <p>University IP ranges can be allowlisted to reduce unnecessary challenges for campus users.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tradeoff-card">
        <h4>💬 Transparency</h4>
        <p>Clear messaging helps users understand the brief security verification delay.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tradeoff-card">
        <h4>🔒 Privacy</h4>
        <p>Security services must balance threat detection with user privacy, disclosing data practices clearly.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="poster-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Key Takeaways</h2>
    <div class="takeaways-list">
      <div class="takeaway-item">
        <div class="takeaway-num">1</div>
        <div class="takeaway-text">Bot traffic represents nearly half of all requests to academic publisher websites.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="takeaway-item">
        <div class="takeaway-num">2</div>
        <div class="takeaway-text">Multi-stage CDN-edge verification pipelines block the majority of malicious bots with minimal impact on human users.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="takeaway-item">
        <div class="takeaway-num">3</div>
        <div class="takeaway-text">Quantitative monitoring using traceable identifiers like Ray IDs enables continuous optimization of the security-usability balance.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="takeaway-item">
        <div class="takeaway-num">4</div>
        <div class="takeaway-text">Collaboration between publishers and CDN providers is critical for sustaining open, secure access to scientific knowledge.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <footer class="poster-footer">
    <span>IEEE Symposium on Security and Privacy</span>
    <span class="venue-badge">S&P 2026</span>
    <span>Source: Science.org / AAAS Case Study</span>
  </footer>
</div>

